- Custom parameters are enclosed in braces ({{}}). Spaces and line breaks before and after the parameter names within the braces are ignored.
- You can specify a maximum of 20 custom parameters.
- A custom parameter name can contain only letters, digits, hyphens (-), and underscores (_). Parameter names are not case-sensitive.
- A custom parameter name cannot exceed 64 bytes in length.

This parameter is required.', example='ifconfig -s'),
  description?: string(name='Description', description='The description of the command. All characters are supported. The description cannot exceed 512 characters in length.', example='test'),
  enableParameter?: boolean(name='EnableParameter', description='Specifies whether the created command uses custom parameters.

Default value: false.', example='false'),
  name?: string(name='Name', description='The name of the command. All characters are supported. The name cannot exceed 128 characters in length.

This parameter is required.', example='testName'),
  regionId?: string(name='RegionId', description='The region ID. You can call [ListRegions](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/189315.html) to query available regions.

This parameter is required.', example='cn-hangzhou'),
